{"title":"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is a regular pentagon. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb96fd4db40cba2f114e6b03472a55682ea2dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP, AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201e0f38191233f52b0d395bda64be69e9b831b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> are the perpendiculars dropped from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f753072848b550ab96753e80e9cc829bde6329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD, CB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> extended and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> extended, \nrespectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the pentagon. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a560c081bbbeb6c156b50e6de7f972fb399b1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a32b8333090ebbf1b47a46394807f2170dfdc50a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO + AQ + AR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4a282f655baace8a8bd02799266f80bb34198c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); pair O=origin, A=2*dir(90), B=2*dir(18), C=2*dir(306), D=2*dir(234), E=2*dir(162), P=(C+D)/2, Q=C+3.10*dir(C--B), R=D+3.10*dir(D--E), S=C+4.0*dir(C--B), T=D+4.0*dir(D--E); draw(A--B--C--D--E--A^^E--T^^B--S^^R--A--Q^^A--P^^rightanglemark(A,Q,S)^^rightanglemark(A,R,T)); dot(O); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,dir(B)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(O+P)/2,W); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,dir(B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,dir(C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,dir(D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,dir(E)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,dir(P)); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,dir(Q)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,dir(R)); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"545\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9598aaa31d9a77eb7a78a5508967cc5fec6728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 + \\sqrt{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2 + \\sqrt{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"441\" height=\"21\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To solve the problem, we compute the area of regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> in two different ways. First, we can divide regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> into five congruent triangles.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa585bf7d802319fcf678dba1c6685da986bb22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, O, P, Q, R;  A = dir(90); B = dir(90 - 360/5); C = dir(90 - 2*360/5); D = dir(90 - 3*360/5); E = dir(90 - 4*360/5); O = (0,0); P = (C + D)/2; Q = (A + reflect(B,C)*(A))/2; R = (A + reflect(D,E)*(A))/2;  draw((2*R - E)--D--C--(2*Q - B)); draw(A--P); draw(A--Q); draw(A--R); draw(B--A--E); draw((O--B),dashed); draw((O--C),dashed); draw((O--D),dashed); draw((O--E),dashed);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(0)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, W); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, NE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, S); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, Q, dir(0)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, W); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (O + P)/2, dir(0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the side length of the regular pentagon, then each of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd97737c9a1eb5146725902d4e4c4bda1388129b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d9b534de592b2a7fc63b97e1f0faab799204e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4097e707215c7c2085c3fd539de4c228d44f1880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f433b683ff8ceb019b8940b8a8c403afb6656e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7c877fb5b479fe0502a5c7790b7f14506e7498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EOA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and height 1, so the area of regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b20ea938fb0684c0aacef9ff98b57bb4128268cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5s/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we divide regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> into triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f58ee27d67000adcb3c6e7084604a6065c3db1e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, O, P, Q, R;  A = dir(90); B = dir(90 - 360/5); C = dir(90 - 2*360/5); D = dir(90 - 3*360/5); E = dir(90 - 4*360/5); O = (0,0); P = (C + D)/2; Q = (A + reflect(B,C)*(A))/2; R = (A + reflect(D,E)*(A))/2;  draw((2*R - E)--D--C--(2*Q - B)); draw(A--P); draw(A--Q); draw(A--R); draw(B--A--E); draw(A--C,dashed); draw(A--D,dashed);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(0)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, W); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, dir(0)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, S); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, Q, dir(0)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, W); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (O + P)/2, dir(0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\nTriangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfbb613faad8163b72b5f1fee1b4b71ff8adbdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AO + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" />. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201e0f38191233f52b0d395bda64be69e9b831b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the area of regular pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is also\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73e7c6f37b937b1de5515073177326bcfa9094d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{s}{2} (AO + AQ + AR + 1).\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"32\" />\nHence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f65f3411ab806ee49aa9bd902213a700b761b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{s}{2} (AO + AQ + AR + 1) = \\frac{5s}{2},\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"37\" />\nwhich means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d31563d3798099503ef306c78e803f2d8065676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO + AQ + AR + 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"192\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c33d973e0d96a80513d0b0504e874a8e653ccc21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO + AQ + AR = \\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"23\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbbac62a58811f44fda1df541fe2d2b7f43bc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Now, we know that angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c78da75ea2599094769ada56f76cb4a30329a0b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180 \\cdot 3}{5} = 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />. Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/5879caf4ddad58c2151c0519e3fb5c0a6f1d3d21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 54 = \\frac{OP}{DO} = \\frac{1}{DO}, DO = \\frac{1}{\\sin 54}\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"37\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e51574f7fe24ce2c3b025b33cc7870029084aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan 54 = \\frac{OP}{DP} = \\frac{1}{DP}, DP = \\frac{1}{\\tan 54}\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"37\" />Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/6841e129c3cf32332e71bc4a0709a2fc978d54b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2DP = \\frac{2}{\\tan 54}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"37\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e6939e631dd3db3a5cc76f343eef490c123b11bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 72 = \\frac{AQ}{AB} = AQ \\tan 54 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}, AQ = \\frac{2 \\sin 72}{\\tan 54}\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"38\" />Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d76968cc7f872c979c23fd7f49b4f84300e556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO + AQ + AR = AO + 2AQ = \\frac{1}{\\sin 54}+\\frac{4 \\sin 72}{\\tan 54} = \\frac{1}{\\sin 54} + 8 \\sin 36 \\cos 54 = \\frac{1}{\\cos 36} + 8-8\\cos^2(36)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"793\" height=\"37\" />. Recalling that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33889c4e79cf5daa6b9f613d1a90a25458f5189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 36 = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{5}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"41\" /> gives a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME\" title=\"1986 AHSME\">1986 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <